Thx for answer, yes in VER 8 change detection not working, I didn't realize that for Date is not change detection, a little  disappointment, comming from strong type landscape.

Date is Interface so if I do some simple Interface:

```typescript
export interface ObI {
  title: string;
  showDays: number;
}
...
changeDay(event: string): void {
    if (event === 'today') {
      this.obI.title = 'today';
    } else if (event === 'previous') {     
      this.obI.title = 'previous';
    } else if (event === 'next') {
      this.obI.title = 'next';
    }
```

```html
<h1>
    Welcome to {{ obI.title }}!
  </h1>
```
Then change detection is working so where is from language point difference?

Even if I use ChangeDetectorRef and this.cdr.detectChanges() still not working, this is totally irrational, so for some interfaces work and for some not.

